<http://data.silknow.org/object/7db01982-c5c9-3f49-8219-f1e56469c49c/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Bedspread made of three widths of material; silk lampas; light blue ground with design, in taupe and ivory silk wefts, of be-ribboned poodles dancing on scrolls, Vulcan at forge, sea horse and fountain, swags, trophies of war, caduceus, etc.; border, sewed on all four sides, of rinceau with serpents and caryatids on sides; in each corner a lion's head; only center panel unseamed; slightly faded in irregular areas; trimmed on all four edges with pale blue and ivory silk galloon; lined with ivory taffeta; cracked in many places."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/7db01982-c5c9-3f49-8219-f1e56469c49c> .

